eSPX agent rules index

Client docs (humans): `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`, `docs/MULTI_REGION.md`, `docs/MILESTONE.md`.

Agent rules: `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — follow scoped rules whose `globs` match files you edit.

`espx.mdc`: Always — SLA, layout, hot-path summary
`code-style.mdc`: Go, Lua, SQL structure and PR gates
`hot-path.mdc`: `internal/ingestion`, tracker ingest
`load-test-bpf.mdc`: Perf validation: BPF + Prometheus, load tests
`data-layer.mdc`: Redis, Postgres, ClickHouse, migrations
`control-plane.mdc`: management, outbox, admin APIs
`rtb.mdc`: In-process auction, OpenRTB
`edge.mdc`: nginx Lua, XDP programs
`compliance.mdc`: Defensive perimeter, XDP policy
`chaos.mdc`: Fault injection, chaos tests
`service-boundaries.mdc`: cmd/* imports and ownership
`open-gaps.mdc`: Routes to `docs/MILESTONE.md` backlog
`capabilities.mdc`: Routing to client vs agent docs

Precedence: `espx.mdc` SLA and alloc rules on `/track`; `code-style.mdc` on structure; `service-boundaries.mdc` on imports; `load-test-bpf.mdc` before claiming perf improvements.
